{"t": 1794111581.8225813, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Pipeline fix for `main` (pipeline #8812, job `test:contract` #77104)\n\n**Root cause.** The contract job fails on `contract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format`:\n\n```\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE   AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n`billing/invoice.py` interpolated the sequence with plain `{seq}`, so the sequence part was never padded. The finance ERP import contract (FIN-77) requires the sequence to be zero-padded to 6 digits.\n\n**Fix.** Format the sequence as `{seq:06d}`:\n\n```python\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\n**Verification.** Ran the contract test locally against the patched module: `1 passed`. The `lint` job was already green, so with `test:contract` passing the main-branch pipeline is green again. The ERP v2 format must keep this 6-digit zero padding, otherwise the finance ERP import breaks.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
